Version-pin fix. In 54ec328 I added @tauri-apps/api with range ^2, which npm resolved to 2.11.1 — but the Rust tauri crate is 2.10.3 (Cargo.lock), and the tauri CLI aborts the build on a major/minor mismatch ('Found version mismatched Tauri packages'). First installer build failed there. Pinned to ~2.10.0 (resolves 2.10.1) so it tracks the crate's minor and can't drift to 2.11 on a fresh install. If the Rust tauri minor is ever bumped, bump this in lockstep. Installer then built clean: cargo build -p xpressclaw-cli --features android (release), sidecar copied, tauri build produced fresh nsis .exe + msi at 12:05. Also note for future: the build.ps1 background run failed once with 'not recognized' because the PowerShell process started outside the repo root — build.ps1 uses relative paths (frontend\build, target\release, crates\...) so it MUST run with cwd = repo root; prepend Set-Location when launching it detached.
